.TH EDITRC 5 "February 2026" "Substrate" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
editrc \- editline startup configuration file
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B editrc
file configures behavior of applications that use
.BR editline (3).
.PP
Each non-empty line contains one command and arguments. Lines beginning
with
.B #
are comments.
.PP
The parser uses shell-like tokenization rules for whitespace and quoting.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.editrc
Per-user editline configuration.
.TP
.B /etc/editrc
System-wide default configuration.
.SH COMMANDS
Common commands include:
.TP
.BI "bind " key " " command
Bind a key sequence to an editor command.
.TP
.BI "editor " mode
Set editing mode, typically
.B emacs
or
.BR vi .
.TP
.BI "settc " cap " " value
Set terminal capability override.
.TP
.BI "setty " mode
Apply tty mode preset.
.TP
.BI "history " op " ..."
Configure history behavior (size, uniqueness, load/save).
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
# Use vi key bindings
editor vi

# Keep 1000 commands and avoid adjacent duplicates
history size 1000
history unique on

# Common key bindings
bind "^A" beginning-of-line
bind "^E" end-of-line
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR editline (3),
.BR el_source (3),
.BR history (3)
